{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789549150,"nonce":"5AHkcnVtogbzMWP3Xt9dgvVlXM8=","title":"Boxed set ordering and min(set) break meteor solver","message":"The meteor-contest kernel now builds the correct 2,459 footprints, but its solver initially produced zero solutions. A footprint read from the nested footprint list and a free-board frozenset both reported type `set`; the footprint was a subset of the free board, but `fp \u003c= free` returned False. Dynamic ordering used sequence comparison, so a subset such as `{0,1,2,3,8}` compared against `frozenset(range(50))` failed at the fifth element. This differs from Python set inclusion semantics. A dynamic set passed to `min()` also raised `TypeError: expected a list, got set`.\n\nMinimal dynamic comparison reproducer:\n\n    def compare(a, b):\n        print(a \u003c= b, a \u003c b, b \u003e= a, b \u003e a)\n    compare(frozenset([0, 1, 2, 3, 8]), frozenset(range(50)))\n\nCPython prints `True True True True`; zypy printed `False False False False`. Once corrected, an explicit answer check for the unmodified meteor-contest kernel produces 60 solutions with the same first and last solution as CPython.","files":null}]}